<<<
+ improve makes improvable; see MUTE E. improvisator. Pronounce impro’vizator. Italian form -vvisatore pron. -ahtor’i, fem. -vvisatrice pron. -ahtre’cha, pl. -ori pron. -or’é, -ici pron. -é’ché. improvise, not -ize, see -ISE; i. makes -isable, see MUTE E. impuissant. For pronunciation see PUISSANT.
===
+ **improve** makes *improvable*; see ^^MUTE E^^.

**improvisator.** Pronounce ĭmprŏ'vīzātor. Italian form *-vvisatore* pron. -ahtor'ĭ, fem. *-vvisatrice* pron. -ahtrē'chā, pl. *-ori* pron. -or'ē, *-ici* pron. -ē'chē.

**improvise,** not *-ize*, see ^^-ISE^^; *i.* makes *-isable*, see ^^MUTE E^^.

**impuissant.** For pronunciation see ^^PUISSANT^^.
>>>

<<<
in. The combinations inasmuch as, in order that or to, in so far, in that, & in toto, are taken separately in their alphabetical places.
===
**in.** The combinations *inasmuch as, in order that* or *to, in so far, in that,* & *in toto,* are taken separately in their alphabetical places.
>>>

<<<
inacceptable. Un- is better; see IN- & UN-.
