<<<
brought into the field against her. Though it is true that adequate & inadequate originally meant made & not made equal, & therefore might be & were followed by to with any suitable noun or infinitive, modern
===
brought into the field against her.* Though it is true that *adequate* & *inadequate* originally meant made & not made equal, & therefore might be & were followed by *to* with any suitable noun or infinitive, modern
>>>

<<<
vague additions like to the need, to the occasion, to the task, are still possible,
===
vague additions like *to the need, to the occasion, to the task,* are still possible,
>>>

<<<
or like His revenues were found inadequate to his expences (Gibbon) or Is language adequate to describe it? (W. Collins) are abandonments
===
or like *His revenues were found inadequate to his expences* (Gibbon) or *Is language adequate to describe it?* (W. Collins) are abandonments
>>>

<<<
that has taken place between adequate & equal, inadequate & unequal. His resources were inadequate, or inadequate to the occasion, but not inadequate to those of his opponent, nor to take or taking the town.
===
that has taken place between *adequate* & *equal, inadequate* & *unequal.* *His resources were inadequate,* or *inadequate to the occasion,* but not *inadequate to those of his opponent,* nor *to take* or *taking the town.*
>>>

